summary:
  Any station with the word somewhere in its name stands ahead of the genre.

history:
  A station leads a genre's list only when it is named after the word: take
  the station words and the bare numbers out of "Rock FM 104.6" and what is
  left is "rock". "Rock Antenne" has a name of its own and stands in the
  list on its votes. A contains-match puts them all in front again.

target:
  package/contents/ui/SearchLogic.js

find:
      return rest.join("") === want.join("");

replace:
      return rest.join("").indexOf(want.join("")) !== -1;

expect:
  Killed by tst_searchlogic::test_a_station_named_after_the_word_leads.
  Line-neutral.
